ir observer members are full  members and it also creates an  environment where observer members can  gain access to some of the vendors  within the industry some of the  suppliers but in the industry some of  the contractors within the industry in a  non-commercial environment where people  are not trying to sell to them they're  sharing information on a neutral basis  which is extremely valuable for them and  finally I think ultimately if they take  on board the interaction they can have  with other observer members other  operators who've already embarked on  this farmer to the home mission and have  a lot of experience and knowledge that  they can share again in a very open and  friendly environment the benefits it's  very difficult to put a value on those  benefits from a their priceless  indeed it really was a fantastic success  one of the most successful conferences  we've had to date if I look at the  caliber of attendees it's significantly  increased over the last few years and in  particular last year what we saw was  really strong representation from the  operator community and this clearly  reflects the activity that we're seeing  out there in the industry where they're  out there actually building fiber  networks they're connecting people to  those networks and as a result they need  to get their employees exposed to the  broader fiber-to-the-home industry and  understand what the key innovations are  that are happening within the industry  who the key suppliers of equipment and  solutions are and really to learn the  lessons from the speakers at the  conference where they're sharing  valuable insights into their experience  in deployment  council it was a very easy decision for  us to make if we look at the sheer level  of investment that's going on in the  French market and fiber-to-the-home they  can be held up there amongst a small  handful of others within Europe as the  shining light for fiber-to-the-home  investment the sheer level of engagement 